      "statusChangeID": "641877f133b2040c942f4f09",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Hi, this is not a bug but a change in the fly mode feature for the camera. Previously, due to both \"take a picture\" and \"tilt\" competing for the trigger button users were accidentally taking photos when they only intended to pitch/roll the lens forward/backward to change the angle. To prevent this conflict we added the \"Trigger to take photo\" toggle so users can control which action happens on holding trigger when in fly mode.\n\nEven when you have it off (trigger changes tilt), you can still take photos with the timer or photo buttons in the camera UI. If you prefer the classic trigger shot, you can keep the toggle on.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-17T02:41:12.857Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "`1.) Open photo camera`\n\n`2.) Switch to fly mode and move lens away`\n\n`3.) Hold camera phone then press trigger, observe no photo taken`\n\n`4.) Open behavior settings then toggle on 'Trigger to take photo'`\n\n`5.) Hold camera phone again and press trigger, photo taken`",
